<title>JORDAN: Jordan bank sector Aug foreign assets rise 2.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Jordan bank sector Aug foreign assets rise 2.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>AMMAN 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Jordanian banking sector's net foreign assets, including central bank holdings, rose 2.5 percent in August to 4.152 billion dinars ($5.9 billion) from the previous month, the Central Bank's latest monthly bulletin said.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of dinars)</p>
<p>				 Aug 96  July 96  Aug 95 1995   1994</p>
<p>  * Total foreign assets  4,152   4,050   3,880   4,068  3,586</p>
<p> ** Foreign assets	  1,844   1,781   1,809   1,883  1,682</p>
<p>*** Central Bank assets   2,308   2,269   2,071   2,185  1,904</p>
<p>NOTE - Source: Jordan Central Bank monthly bulletin. (*) includes both Central Bank holdings along with foreign currency deposits held with foreign banks abroad and non-resident foreign currency deposits. (**) Private bank assets that excludes Central Bank holdings with most of the funds composed of accounts invested with foreign banks. (***) includes a 35 percent compulsory reserve requirement imposed on banks' foreign currency deposits.</p>
<p>$1=0.7080 dinar</p>
<p>- Amman newsroom, 962 6 623 776</p>
